 "notes": "1973 late-modern face-brick corner block at Beach. Red-brown face brick; a corbelled brick belt with a dentil row over the street storey; upper storeys are a brick pier frame with deep balconies: dark timber soffits and vertical-slat rails on a projecting deck, large dark plate glass set 1.2 m back; street storey mostly solid brick with deep-set dark windows and the recessed dark entry at the Hyde corner. Edges 1, 3 and 6 dressed as street faces (edgeRoles flank + streetEdges). Face brick #964e3c, upper frame/rails/decks near-black charcoal, low picture windows (sill 1.0 m, 1.4 m tall). Brick #87473a, balcony boxes in dark-stained wood #3a2e27 (lum lifted off black); brick/corbel/piers/corner entry/dark glazing already present; storey count kept (roll 4, LiDAR 12.95). Brick nudged to #87473a. Balcony boxes, dentil belt, dark glass, recessed corner entry already present. Brick, dentil/corbel belt wrapping the corner, recessed corner entry, dark glazing already present. Applied: solid dark-timber balcony guards (rail solid) instead of thin bars, ground picture windows single-pane (paneM 20, no mullion grid). Tint lift (2026-10-02): paint tints lifted toward the sunlit paint (t' = 1-(1-t)k); brick tints converted to target / kit colour.",
